<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Przemysł II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1257–<a href="/years/1296">1296</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Przemysł II was duke of Greater <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> who gained <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomerelia">Pomerelia</a> in 1294 and was crowned King of Poland at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gniezno">Gniezno</a> in 1295, the first royal coronation in Poland for over two centuries. He was murdered at Rogoźno in February 1296, probably by agents of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a>, and his lands passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wladyslaw-i-lokietek">Władysław the Elbow-high</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/przemysl-ii.jpg" alt="Przemysł II" width="320" height="277" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anonymous plate · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Seal_of_Przemys%C5%82_II_King_of_Poland_from_1296.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
